From: CatOS Package Maintainers <packages@catos.info>
Subject: [PATCH] build: remove build-machine CPU tuning from release builds

Distribution packages must run on machines other than the builder. Keep the
remaining release flags, but let the distribution toolchain select the target
ISA through CFLAGS and CXXFLAGS.

---
 meson.build | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 3db7adb..60e1d30 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -16,6 +16,5 @@
 if get_option('buildtype') == 'release'
   add_project_arguments(
-    '-march=native', '-mtune=native',
     '-fomit-frame-pointer', '-ffunction-sections', '-fdata-sections',
     language: ['c', 'cpp'],
   )
